=='''Administrative divisions'''==
The Association of East-Asia is divided into 60 provinces, and one capital district, each overseen by an elected governor, legislature and provincial court system. Each province is further divided into prefectures, municipalities and villages. The provinces enjoy a degree of autonomy comparable to American states or the provincial system adopted near the end of the United Federation of China.
